: classify dup 0 > if "+" . else dup 0 < if "-" . else "z" . then then drop ;
5 classify cr
-5 classify cr
0 classify cr
: countdown 0 begin 1 + dup . dup 3 = until drop cr ;
countdown
: tagged 0 begin 1 + dup . dup 4 = if drop exit then again ;
tagged cr

\ a closer with no matching opener errors instead of patching an arbitrary
\ dictionary cell (a bare `200 then` once silently wrote dict[200]); each line
\ is its own REPL entry, and the dictionary stays intact afterward
200 then
200 else
200 until
200 200 repeat
3 4 + . cr

\ an opener outside a definition or quotation errors instead of silently
\ emitting nothing (the guarded body used to run regardless of the test)
0 if "unreachable" . then
?if "unreachable" . then
begin 1 until
5 5 + . cr

\ an unterminated conditional (an if/else with no matching then) fails at
\ compile time and discards the half-built word, instead of compiling a branch
\ with an unpatched offset that dispatches through a null handler at runtime;
\ the system keeps compiling afterward
: bad-if 0 if 5 ;
bad-if
: bad-else 1 if 2 else 3 ;
bad-else
: bad-qif [: 0 if 5 :] execute ;
bad-qif
6 7 + . cr
